{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Hanging out With Friends", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Remember When ... ?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Used to and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>  have  similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "However, when <span class=\"strong\">would</span> replaces <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>, the same example becomes ungrammatical:<br><br>  <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India.</span> (not correct)<br> <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I used to go out with a guy before I left for culinary school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we were in high school, Ted would write me poems and send me flowers every week.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.<br/>Phrasal verbs can either be separable or inseparable.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The object of a phrasal verb can go either between the verb and the preposition or after the preposition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I handed in my homework. <br/>I handed my homework in.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the object of the sentence is a pronoun, it must go between the two parts of the phrasal verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I handed it in.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some phrasal verbs are inseparable, so the verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span> </li></ul><ul><li>take off = leave the ground <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The plane took off on time.</span></li></ul><ul><li>look out = beware! be careful!  <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li></ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to break up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to end a relationship\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to turn out\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to become clear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to go out with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to be in a relationship with someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to grow apart\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to become different\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to settle down\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to establish a permanent situation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to work out\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to have a successful outcome\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to patch up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to repair, to fix\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to get back together\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to reunite after a breakup\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: He turned out to be a boring boyfriend. Our relationship wasn't working out. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: You should patch things up with him.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to break up", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to end a relationship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why did you guys break up in the end?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about relationships.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to grow apart ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to become different from one another in a relationship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We realized that we were growing apart.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get back together", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reunite after a breakup", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We tried to get back together, but it didn't work out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to patch up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to repair; to fix", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope you patch things up with Marco.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to settle down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to establish a permanent situation, usually in a relationship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He wanted to settle down, but I wasn't ready.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rocky ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "uneasy; difficult", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our relationship is a bit rocky at the moment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "smooth sailing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "easy; without problems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Relationships aren't always smooth sailing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine you are a journalist writing about relationships.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give advice on relationships and friendships, using your experience and memories as examples.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a newspaper column (10-14 lines) about relationships.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use phrasal verbs and habits in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your column aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about relationships and friendships.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about habits in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about actions related to friendships and relationships.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le01ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le01ob02re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn7le01ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn7le01ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        What's on your mind, V? You look worried.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    Don't worry about it. It's just Marco. Our relationship is a little rocky at the moment. We argue all the time. I don't get it. We used to agree on everything!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        Relationships aren't always smooth sailing. I remember when I used to date that guy in high school. He was so sweet at the beginning. He would write me poems and send me flowers. I used to think it was the most romantic thing anyone  ever did for me.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn7le01ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    What happened? Why did you guys break up in the end?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        He turned out to be a very boring boyfriend! We didn't really have anything in common. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    I know the feeling. I used to go out with a guy before I left for culinary school. We would try to find things that we both liked to do,     but it became harder and harder. We realized that we were growing apart. He wanted to settle down, but I wasn't ready.", "id": 2, "time": "31000"}, {"image": "engenn7le01ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        I remember that boyfriend. You used to really like him!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    I did. We tried to get back together, but it didn't work out. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        Well, you should try to patch up things with Marco.", "id": 3, "time": "55000"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about friendships and relationships.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about habits in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about actions related to relationships and key life events. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you have a favorite memory from elementary school? From high school?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What are the qualities you would like to see in a boyfriend or girlfriend?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you think friendships are important in your life? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Let's take a trip down memory lane!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "qu